# Deliberately narrow: only paths whose bytes on disk are load-bearing.
# No `* text=auto` line — that would renormalize the whole tree.

# Generated JSON artifacts are byte-compared against freshly generated output by
# `--check` gates. The generators emit LF, so a CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true,
# the Windows default) would fail those gates for reasons unrelated to drift.
*.json text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must reach Linux CI and git-bash with LF; CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
